{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530151-is-white-wolf-paradox-stealing-art-now","id":1530151,"title":"Is White Wolf / Paradox stealing Art Now?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-07T04:09:30-08:00","id":1530151,"title":"Is White Wolf / Paradox stealing Art Now?","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/manyworldsofdarkness/741587775949783040\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://64.media.tumblr.com/bf52b35c0a06accc5d4e9aa5df6284e7/8b7dc46830e37f11-29/s200x200u_c1/64157bf38937f870f3ddba084202672c8e0824ca.pnj\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/manyworldsofdarkness/741587775949783040\" target=\"_blank\"> Reblog by @manyworldsofdarkness </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/manyworldsofdarkness/741587775949783040\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.tumblr.com/manyworldsofdarkness/741587775949783040 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> \ud83d\udcac 38&nbsp;&nbsp;\ud83d\udd01 212&nbsp;&nbsp;\u2764\ufe0f 227&nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;'Vamily Spotlight': WoD Brand Team is Taking Art Without Permission&nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;Recently, I was informed by a friend that some work of mine had shown up in the World of Darkness&rsquo; offici&hellip; </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T05:30:59-08:00","id":1530154,"title":"","content":"Now? They've been doing it for awhile. Werewolf had a big issue where readers found numerous pictures where the artist had traced real life people and photographs without getting permission from, or informing those people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T06:19:21-08:00","id":1530156,"title":"","content":"* sigh * ...<br /> <br /> Not surprised to find out that the Vamily-Spotlight as a segment is getting expanded by somebody just grabbing random WOD-fanart without informing the creators. The WOD-news-show used to be hosted by Outstar alone and the ratio was like 90% news and 10% &quot;Vamily spotlight&quot;. She brought on Hubby as a cohost and in addition to that, the ratio has become 30% news and 70% &quot;Vamily spotlight.&quot;. Bringing Hubby on was an improvement but in terms of content, the WOD-news-show-streams are boring. You don't have the interviews with creators anymore. And so the news-portion often feels like Outstar reciting stuff I could also just read in a press-release. And it doesn't surprise me that the show doesn't have enough of a following to support the Vamily-segment by submissions alone. Renegade are doing their own online-stuff (including the WOD-books they write) and so at this point, Outstar's show is in this forlorn position. I bet you if you were to make a list of the most popular WOD-online-projects you'd get a ton of fan-projects first and Outstar's WOD-news-show wouldn't even crack the Top 10.<br /> <br /> And then you get to the unforced error of mishandling the Vamily Spotlight. Since this is an official corporate-supported show, the burden of handling fan-art should be much higher. When a fan-project features fan-art without the proper procedure of asking for permission and giving them a link in the description of the YT-video, it's an &quot;oopsie&quot;. It's bad. You shouldn't do that. But with a fan-project I think it's enough for those people to apologize and do better. Outstar's WOD-news-show is an <i>official </i>show paid for by Paradox. It doesn't seem like Outstar is receiving a lot of support from Paradox but she's the public face of this problem. There were previous instances where I think the actual problem is Paradox as a company mishandling the management of the IP but it's Outstar as the public face of that mismanagement. And so the anger is all directed towards her. Luckily I'm not in her position but it is what it is. This will be yet another thing to point at as the mistake-laden handling of the WOD-IP by Paradox and their misguided interaction with the fan-community.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T08:45:25-08:00","id":1530165,"title":"","content":"I may be missing something but isn't displaying the art and discussing on the segment just reviewing it? It's not stealing it.<br /> <br /> &quot;My publicly available art is being talked about in public!&quot;<br /> <br /> There's also a very, uh, &quot;I hate V5 and this is a V5 show so this is wrong!&quot; energy to that post. Mind you, it IS Tumbler.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 02-07-2024, 11:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T08:50:34-08:00","id":1530166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530151-is-white-wolf-paradox-stealing-art-now?p=1530165#post1530165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may be missing something but isn't displaying the art and discussing on the segment just reviewing it? It's not stealing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the main issue here is that the videos are monetized. So, in fact, they earn some money with content that was taken by others without their permission.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think it's bad form to just collect and display fan art without contacting the artists. Most of the time, when official YT channels display fan art (like Star Wars etc.), it's fan art that was sent to them. What if the artist never wanted this sort of attention in the first place?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T08:57:53-08:00","id":1530168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caldorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530151-is-white-wolf-paradox-stealing-art-now?p=1530166#post1530166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the main issue here is that the videos are monetized. So, in fact, they earn some money with content that was taken by others without their permission.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think it's bad form to just collect and display fan art without contacting the artists. Most of the time, when official YT channels display fan art (like Star Wars etc.), it's fan art that was sent to them. What if the artist never wanted this sort of attention in the first place?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, yes, but...so are reviews of movies.<br /> <br /> This argument means you think if you review STAR WARS: RISE OF SKYWALKER and get enough views to make some money then Disney is entitled to some of that -- which is ridiculous. I run a fantasy review site and what little is made from our efforts goes to the maintenance of the site and community we've made. The only real money to be made in Youtubing is Patreon and that is very hit or miss.<br /> <br /> I think part of this is also notable that I have my own feelings on this. They displayed some of my memes and creations on the show as well and didn't inform me.<br /> <br /> But my reaction was just ANNOYANCE.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 02-07-2024, 12:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T09:16:04-08:00","id":1530171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530151-is-white-wolf-paradox-stealing-art-now?p=1530165#post1530165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may be missing something but isn't displaying the art and discussing on the segment just reviewing it? It's not stealing it.<br /> <br /> &quot;My publicly available art is being talked about in public!&quot;<br /> <br /> There's also a very, uh, &quot;I hate V5 and this is a V5 show so this is wrong!&quot; energy to that post. Mind you, it IS Tumbler.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, there's a lot wrong with this description that completely misunderstands the situation.<ul><li>The WOD-news-shows are monetized videos and the creators mentioned in the Vamily-segment don't see any money. The least one can do is to show the creators in that segment some courtesy.</li> <li>The art may be publicly available but these days there are multiple platforms where artists post their work and maybe they have a preference for where you should go to find their work or maybe the artist has a Patreon (with a paid subscription) or other sites that sell digital art. So when their art is getting featured on a show, rather than the show just showing their post they might want to also mention their Patreon or another venue they use to sell their art. And it would be right thing to do to allow them to present these links to those venues during the show in return for allowing the WOD-news-show to show their art.</li> <li>If you're just copy-pasting a post with art that you found somewhere without talking to the artist, I see one obvious problem: What if the post you're using stole art from someone else? Of course, you wouldn't know that if you just grabbed stuff from the internet without talking to the artist. But that's another reason why you should check in with the actual artist first. Not just for the sake of courtesy but also because you don't want to accidentally promote someone who stole art. They're lucky this hasn't happened yet.</li> <li>I often hear this &quot;grognard&quot;-talk of &quot;That guy just hates WOD5E&quot; as a way to frame criticism of current WOD-products and actions by Paradox/Renegade and it bugs me to no end. This kind of argument is a waste of space. This kind of edition-warring doesn't add anything worthwhile to any discussion. There are people who have preferrences when it comes to 20th Anniversary, CofD and WOD5E. But it's idiotic the moment this gets turned into some kind of tool of character-assassination. You're not gonna change the facts by just turning to fan-club-lingo.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T09:24:35-08:00","id":1530174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530151-is-white-wolf-paradox-stealing-art-now?p=1530171#post1530171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm, there's a lot wrong with this description that completely misunderstands the situation.<ul><li>The WOD-news-shows are monetized videos and the creators mentioned in the Vamily-segment don't see any money. The least one can do is to show the creators in that segment some courtesy.</li> <li>The art may be publicly available but these days there are multiple platforms where artists post their work and maybe they have a preference for where you should go to find their work or maybe the artist has a Patreon (with a paid subscription) or other sites that sell digital art. So when their art is getting featured on a show, rather than the show just showing their post they might want to also mention their Patreon or another venue they use to sell their art. And it would be right thing to do to allow them to present these links to those venues during the show in return for allowing the WOD-news-show to show their art.</li> <li>If you're just copy-pasting a post with art that you found somewhere without talking to the artist, I see one obvious problem: What if the post you're using stole art from someone else? Of course, you wouldn't know that if you just grabbed stuff from the internet without talking to the artist. But that's another reason why you should check in with the actual artist first. Not just for the sake of courtesy but also because you don't want to accidentally promote someone who stole art. They're lucky this hasn't happened yet.</li> <li>I often hear this &quot;grognard&quot;-talk of &quot;That guy just hates WOD5E&quot; as a way to frame criticism of current WOD-products and actions by Paradox/Renegade and it bugs me to no end. This kind of argument is a waste of space. This kind of edition-warring doesn't add anything worthwhile to any discussion. There are people who have preferrences when it comes to 20th Anniversary, CofD and WOD5E. But it's idiotic the moment this gets turned into some kind of tool of character-assassination. You're not gonna change the facts by just turning to fan-club-lingo.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the thing, though.<br /> <br /> 1. It's monetized the same way that every other reviewer is. Disney doesn't get any money from a girl reviewing Moana.<br /> <br /> 2. This is the definition of fair use, though. A few minutes on a show where something is discussed is something that virtually all art is covered by. This would prevent discussing things like Skyrim mods or other fan made content on many platforms.<br /> <br /> 3. I mean, it's sharing the art and discussing it. It's requires you to accept the premise that you're taking from them by sharing it.<br /> <br /> 4. If you think I'm dismissing their claim because of grognard talk, I remind you that I'm just drawing it from the poster who said this:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><b>Additionally I would like to note that all of my World of Darkness fanworks are based on legacy books; Vampire 20th Anniversary Edition, Mage the Ascension 20th Anniversary Edition and Hunter: the Reckoning First Edition most often, though there are appearances from others. You\u2019ll note that not one of these books is the territory of Paradox Interactive or their World of Darkness brand management team-- </b>looks to me like they\u2019ve simply trawled the tag without reading what they\u2019re looking at, which means they certainly didn\u2019t take the time to ask permission to use these works. Not only were these actions tantamount to theft, it was also not even their fanart to begin with. And once again, they\u2019d have known this had they contacted me at all, which they did not. It\u2019s a failure on their part on several levels and not only do I want the videos taken down, I think the community is sorely owed an apology for this frivolous theft of art under the banner of \u2018community content\u2019. I didn\u2019t opt in to having my work taken, and it should not have been assumed that it was okay to take my work just because it\u2019s using a tag they also use!</i><br /> <br /> <br /> So, describe for me how that isn't THEM edition warring.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T09:37:27-08:00","id":1530177,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a>, an honest and well-meaning question: What do you hope to achieve by arguing this with us? Are you interested in convincing us that it isn't a problem? Are you just stating your opinion?<br /> <br /> Is it fair use? I don't know, I'm not a lawyer.<br /> <br /> Is it ethical to take the art of an artist (who is not a megacorp like Disney) and use it without their permission? Personally, I don't think so, but I can understand that others might view it differently. So, even if it were legal, should you do it? I don't think so because it's not nice.<br /> <br /> Fact is, this artist is very upset about it. For him, it's real. It's obvious from the reactions online that a significant number of people (including some of us) agree. If I were Paradox, that would tell me that I should change my behavior, not only because it would be very easy to do, but also because it wouldn't upset potential fans and customers.<br /> <br /> (As an aside: I think the review comparison doesn't really work because reviewing a book or movie never displays the whole work, unlike the art presented here.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T09:48:00-08:00","id":1530179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530151-is-white-wolf-paradox-stealing-art-now?p=1530174#post1530174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the thing, though.<br /> 1. It's monetized the same way that every other reviewer is. Disney doesn't get any money from a girl reviewing Moana.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, that comparison sucks... The comparison would be a reviewer of a Disney-fan's art... who is paid by Disney itself! That's a very different category of &quot;Youtuber&quot;... I mean, &quot;Youtuber&quot; doesn't even qualify. Outstar is a corporate employee with an official position producing a corporate-supported show. She's the furthest thing from being a &quot;Youtuber&quot; as one traditionally would understand the term. Or in other words, the WOD-news-show isn't independent. It's a corporate-product. Again, your comparison doesn't make sense therefore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530151-is-white-wolf-paradox-stealing-art-now?p=1530174#post1530174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. This is the definition of fair use, though. A few minutes on a show where something is discussed is something that virtually all art is covered by. This would prevent discussing things like Skyrim mods or other fan made content on many platforms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you're right. It absolutely does do that. Every video-game-company has the right to copyright every single video of their games if they wanted to. It's just that most companies realized that these streams are good promotion-tools. Sponsoring a Youtuber to play a particular game is a good marketing-tool as they have a captive audience who will then get exposed to the game and then get persuaded to buy the game.<br /> <br /> But technically the video-game-companies could block all of that. Case in point: Nintendo. Who knows what's going on in those dinosaur-brains over there that still produce successes despite themselves... but they absolutely hate digital engagement with the fanbase or stuff like using Youtubers to promote themselves. Just look up Smash-Bros tournaments, for example.<br /> <br /> So, yes, an artist could block the appearance of his originally produced art via DMCA.<br /> <br /> Also, this doesn't discount my argument of courtesy. All you're saying so far is that you personally think acting like an asshole is the better way to go in your opinion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530151-is-white-wolf-paradox-stealing-art-now?p=1530174#post1530174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. I mean, it's sharing the art and discussing it. It's requires you to accept the premise that you're taking from them by sharing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the vamily-segments fall far short of any sort of actual review. So this point doesn't make any sense. The Vamily-segment isn't the Siskel &amp; Ebert show, you know...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530151-is-white-wolf-paradox-stealing-art-now?p=1530174#post1530174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. If you think I'm dismissing their claim because of grognard talk, I remind you that I'm just drawing it from the poster who said this:<br /> <br /> Additionally I would like to note that all of my World of Darkness fanworks are based on legacy books; Vampire 20th Anniversary Edition, Mage the Ascension 20th Anniversary Edition and Hunter: the Reckoning First Edition most often, though there are appearances from others. You\u2019ll note that not one of these books is the territory of Paradox Interactive or their World of Darkness brand management team-- looks to me like they\u2019ve simply trawled the tag without reading what they\u2019re looking at, which means they certainly didn\u2019t take the time to ask permission to use these works. Not only were these actions tantamount to theft, it was also not even their fanart to begin with. And once again, they\u2019d have known this had they contacted me at all, which they did not. It\u2019s a failure on their part on several levels and not only do I want the videos taken down, I think the community is sorely owed an apology for this frivolous theft of art under the banner of \u2018community content\u2019. I didn\u2019t opt in to having my work taken, and it should not have been assumed that it was okay to take my work just because it\u2019s using a tag they also use!<br /> <br /> <br /> So, describe for me how that isn't THEM edition warring.</div> </div> </div> </div>All I'm seeing is you demonstrating how you missed the forest for the trees. That's his perspective on his art. That it's based <i>only </i>on the legacy-books. Okay... where's the issue here? The emphasis of edition-warring comes from you here. You're distracting from the issue at hand with your edition-warring.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T09:51:39-08:00","id":1530180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530151-is-white-wolf-paradox-stealing-art-now?p=1530154#post1530154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now? They've been doing it for awhile. Werewolf had a big issue where readers found numerous pictures where the artist had traced real life people and photographs without getting permission from, or informing those people.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know about that situation, I was just bringing this to the community's attention after I saw it on reddit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T10:09:57-08:00","id":1530182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caldorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530151-is-white-wolf-paradox-stealing-art-now?p=1530177#post1530177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a>, an honest and well-meaning question: What do you hope to achieve by arguing this with us? Are you interested in convincing us that it isn't a problem? Are you just stating your opinion?</div> </div> </div> </div>My perspective on it is probably influenced by the fact that I review for:<br /> <br /> Grimdark Magazine<br /> Before We Go Blog<br /> Booknest.EU (which created the Camarilla book controversy)<br /> United Federation of Charles<br /> <br /> And in addition to it, I create fan art, memes, and actually am a professional indie author.<br /> <br /> I've been attacked before for my reviews, including by fellow indie authors who did not like my reviews. I am very worried about the idea of being a reviewer and under attack for free discussion of IP.<br /> <br /> Does that make sense?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T10:20:56-08:00","id":1530183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530151-is-white-wolf-paradox-stealing-art-now?p=1530182#post1530182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My perspective on it is probably influenced by the fact that I review for:<br /> <br /> Grimdark Magazine<br /> Before We Go Blog<br /> Booknest.EU (which created the Camarilla book controversy)<br /> United Federation of Charles<br /> <br /> And in addition to it, I create fan art, memes, and actually am a professional indie author.<br /> <br /> I've been attacked before for my reviews, including by fellow indie authors who did not like my reviews. I am very worried about the idea of being a reviewer and under attack for free discussion of IP.<br /> <br /> Does that make sense?</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, thanks for answering. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It absolutely makes sense but, I must be honest with you, I don't think it applies to this topic very much.<br /> <br /> Nobody is arguing that reviewing stuff isn't allowed. As was pointed out eloquently by the others, however, this is a case where a company uses fan art by individual artists without their consent for promotional purposes. They're not reviewing the art, they're not even meaningfully engaging with the art, it's just filler material to pad out their promotional videos. That's not comparable with what you do, and I think everyone will agree with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T10:54:12-08:00","id":1530184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caldorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530151-is-white-wolf-paradox-stealing-art-now?p=1530183#post1530183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> First of all, thanks for answering. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It absolutely makes sense but, I must be honest with you, I don't think it applies to this topic very much.<br /> <br /> Nobody is arguing that reviewing stuff isn't allowed. As was pointed out eloquently by the others, however, this is a case where a company uses fan art by individual artists without their consent for promotional purposes. They're not reviewing the art, they're not even meaningfully engaging with the art, it's just filler material to pad out their promotional videos. That's not comparable with what you do, and I think everyone will agree with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I just feel differently because when they did my meme, they engaged with it quite well.<br /> <br /> 38:20<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/ZiK2jVAxY4M?t=2300\" data-code=\"ZiK2jVAxY4M\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/ZiK2jVAxY4M/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> But hey, I could be a very different example from others.<br /> <br /> They also seemed to engage with the other art pieces. They don't seem to be &quot;promoting&quot; save in their love of the WOD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T12:59:06-08:00","id":1530198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caldorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530151-is-white-wolf-paradox-stealing-art-now?p=1530177#post1530177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it fair use? I don't know, I'm not a lawyer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also not a lawyer, but I will relate a IP lawyer's professional response:<br /> <br /> It's never actually fair use until you prove it in court.<br /> <br /> Fair use is on the person infringing on someone else's copyright to prove as a defense against getting sued. The standards for it are also extremely vague because judges in IP law are granted wide permission to treat each case on its own with far less attention to precedent than other forms of law.<br /> <br /> The major issue from an actual IP law perspective here (morals on profits, permissions, and so on aren't really strong legal arguments) is the IP law concept of &quot;transformation.&quot;<br /> <br /> Transformation means that the new work is taking the older work and &quot;doing&quot; something to it. Reviews add to the public understanding of a work. Parody adds to public engagement as well. Academic copying of copyrighted materials expands human understanding. Etc. &quot;Hey I found this thing online, here it is in total,&quot; is not transformative, because you're not adding to it. &quot;Engagement&quot; isn't adding anything either.<br /> <br /> Of course, IP laws are also considered vastly outdated as they still can't handle sampling in hip hop and rap music properly, let alone how to deal with the Internet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T15:36:42-08:00","id":1530212,"title":"","content":"So, the IP Holders are stealing fan arts by showing them on their own Channel (from which they Will monetize some few dollars, jn the budget of a billion dollar company).<br /> <br /> And they are called out as thieves and being assholes because they promoted content of a fan.<br /> <br /> And that fan thinks not only that Wod20 doesn't belong to Paradox, but also that fan arts of a product are it's own separated property.<br /> <br /> I may be top lenient with Paradox but everything here seems Tumblr drama with unfounded premises.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T16:03:51-08:00","id":1530216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530151-is-white-wolf-paradox-stealing-art-now?p=1530212#post1530212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the IP Holders are stealing fan arts by showing them on their own Channel (from which they Will monetize some few dollars, jn the budget of a billion dollar company).<br /> <br /> And they are called out as thieves and being assholes because they promoted content of a fan.<br /> <br /> And that fan thinks not only that Wod20 doesn't belong to Paradox, but also that fan arts of a product are it's own separated property.<br /> <br /> I may be top lenient with Paradox but everything here seems Tumblr drama with unfounded premises.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much. A company talking about and showing off fan art, based on that company\u2019s intellectual property, is entirely reasonable, particularly in the context we are discussing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T16:08:20-08:00","id":1530217,"title":"","content":"I don't really understand what the issue is here. All that's required here is for an official channel to show some courtesy and treat the fan-artists with respect. Just a quick chat about showing off their work and how they want to be referenced in the official show. It's a bit baffling to me to see arguments in this thread that think exploiting fan-artists and treating them like a faceless stock-image-database is okay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T16:21:04-08:00","id":1530219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530151-is-white-wolf-paradox-stealing-art-now?p=1530217#post1530217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really understand what the issue is here. All that's required here is for an official channel to show some courtesy and treat the fan-artists with respect. Just a quick chat about showing off their work and how they want to be referenced in the official show. It's a bit baffling to me to see arguments in this thread that think exploiting fan-artists and treating them like a faceless stock-image-database is okay.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are showing off art, and referencing the creators of that art, which gets seen for maybe a minute at most. It is okay in a \u201cfair use\u201d sense, and I would not expect Paradox to contact the creator, any more than I would expect the creator to get permission from Paradox to create the fan art\u2026<br /> <br /> (The fan artists seem to understand fair use, when it comes to using someone else\u2019s intellectual property as the hook for their art.)<br /> <br /> So, no-one is being exploited in reality, and it\u2019s just Tumblr drama based around someone\u2019s misplaced sense of self importance. I know this sounds harsh, but, as someone who makes money out of creative work, I do believe that people should make the effort to understand matters like fair use, and their position in the creative economy, once they start making their work visible to others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T16:27:07-08:00","id":1530220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530151-is-white-wolf-paradox-stealing-art-now?p=1530212#post1530212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that fan thinks not only that Wod20 doesn't belong to Paradox, but also that fan arts of a product are it's own separated property.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Fan art is it's own separate property unless Paradox wants to take artists to court and ask the court to transfer ownership to them. Fan art belongs to the artist, not the product it's inspired by.<br /> <br /> 2) Paradox/nWW issued a fan content license (updating the Dark Pack rules), which does give Paradox some rights to fan works made under it. Clearly stating that art wasn't made under that license is important to establishing what rights Paradox has to fan made content (none without going to court)..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T16:30:15-08:00","id":1530221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530151-is-white-wolf-paradox-stealing-art-now?p=1530219#post1530219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is okay in a \u201cfair use\u201d sense,...</div> </div> </div> </div>What as Paradox done that counts as transformative, and thus makes things fair use?<br /> <br /> Stating it clearly falls under fair use, while asserting people need to understand fair use principles, means you should have a simple answer to this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T16:35:27-08:00","id":1530222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530151-is-white-wolf-paradox-stealing-art-now?p=1530220#post1530220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) Fan art is it's own separate property unless Paradox wants to take artists to court and ask the court to transfer ownership to them. Fan art belongs to the artist, not the product it's inspired by.<br /> <br /> 2) Paradox/nWW issued a fan content license (updating the Dark Pack rules), which does give Paradox some rights to fan works made under it. Clearly stating that art wasn't made under that license is important to establishing what rights Paradox has to fan made content (none without going to court)..</div> </div> </div> </div>The first point is pretty unambiguously correct. The artist owns the copyright, which would prevent, for instance, it being used in a published book. The fan content license is, if I remember, fairly specific, so would not generally apply, for instance, to pictures published on a blog or similar.<br /> <br /> But the fact that the art is specifically referencing the intellectual property of Paradox would make a fair use argument pretty strong if the matter ever went to court, or, indeed, another form of adjudication. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T16:39:45-08:00","id":1530223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530151-is-white-wolf-paradox-stealing-art-now?p=1530219#post1530219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They are showing off art, and referencing the creators of that art, which gets seen for maybe a minute at most. It is okay in a \u201cfair use\u201d sense, and I would not expect Paradox to contact the creator, any more than I would expect the creator to get permission from Paradox to create the fan art\u2026<br /> <br /> (The fan artists seem to understand fair use, when it comes to using someone else\u2019s intellectual property as the hook for their art.)<br /> <br /> So, no-one is being exploited in reality, and it\u2019s just Tumblr drama based around someone\u2019s misplaced sense of self importance. I know this sounds harsh, but, as someone who makes money out of creative work, I do believe that people should make the effort to understand matters like fair use, and their position in the creative economy, once they start making their work visible to others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, what you describe is being an asshole. Because here's the thing: It's called fan-art not just because it's art but because it's coming from <i>fans</i>. Why would you argue in favor of treating fans like shit? You talk of self-importance but the position you articulate sounds arrogant as hell and shows a dismissive attitude towards fan-contributions that help an IP establish a presence on the web. You should want to build a friendly rapport with the fan-base. When somebody puts in the work to produce fan-art, the IP-holder's attitude shouldn't be &quot;And now it's mine, you fool!&quot;. The artist in question acted as a fan and wanted to express their appreciation for an IP. So it's only fair to call for some consideration and courtesy when it comes to the interaction with fans. The IP-holder gets something out of the art-work being produced and the least one can do is also treat the artist behind that like a person.<br /> <br /> Besides, your approach is also stupid. Like I mentioned before: If they're just grabbing images from the web and never interact with the artists, how can anyone be sure that even the minimal attribution they did was accurate...? What if somebody just reposted artwork from somebody else on a Tumblr-post without referencing the original artist and then the show only grabbed the repost? They wouldn't know of the mistake until somebody made a post similar to the one this thread is about which would create yet another problematic case-study of mismanagement. You don't just talk to the artists because it's good PR and the proper way to deal with fans. You do it to avoid blunders like presenting art with the wrong attribution. Just grabbing art from the web without talking to the artist is therefore a just plain stupid idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T16:41:22-08:00","id":1530224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530151-is-white-wolf-paradox-stealing-art-now?p=1530221#post1530221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What as Paradox done that counts as transformative, and thus makes things fair use?<br /> <br /> Stating it clearly falls under fair use, while asserting people need to understand fair use principles, means you should have a simple answer to this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, there is a simple answer; it falls under the criticism and comment area of fair use as defined by section 107 of the US Copyright Act. <br /> <br /> (There are actually quite a few avenues for fair use, and a transformation is only one.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T18:32:44-08:00","id":1530233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really shows just how little feel for artists when all that get is side of, &quot;Just be glad to be noticed.&quot; Of course, the same flippancy can apply to the act of getting proper permissions from said artists. They're a big company with far more resources readily available to them than your average artist. No excuse on their part to make the effort to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if the artists were furious if, say, a youtube reviewer were commenting on it?<br /> <br /> Say a channel called ChicagoByNightLover or someone not part of the corporate megastructure?<br /> <br /> I ask because I see a MASSIVE difference between tracing or incorporating art into an official product versus reviewing fan material that is publicly posted.<br /> <br /> And, again, I'm a creator too.<br /> <br /> Serious question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T19:01:06-08:00","id":1530236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530151-is-white-wolf-paradox-stealing-art-now?p=1530233#post1530233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And if the artists were furious if, say, a youtube reviewer were commenting on it?<br /> <br /> Say a channel called ChicagoByNightLover or someone not part of the corporate megastructure?<br /> <br /> I ask because I see a MASSIVE difference between tracing or incorporating art into an official product versus reviewing fan material that is publicly posted.<br /> <br /> And, again, I'm a creator too.<br /> <br /> Serious question.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know how you don't see the obvious issue there. The &quot;MASSIVE difference&quot; you're talking about there is meaningless because it's pretty clear where things land in this case. The WOD-news-show with its vamily-spotlight is an <i>official product</i>. So your scenario of an independent channel called &quot;ChicagoByNightLover&quot; is irrelevant as that isn't what we're talking about.<br /> <br /> And even then, <i>an independent Youtube-channel should also ask for permission first</i> and have some correspondence with an artist before using their art. It's just that official channels should be expected to be even more careful and courteous when it comes to fan-interactions. Because official channels should come with a raised expectation of quality in production and ethical conduct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T19:09:37-08:00","id":1530238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530151-is-white-wolf-paradox-stealing-art-now?p=1530236#post1530236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know how you don't see the obvious issue there. The &quot;MASSIVE difference&quot; you're talking about there is meaningless because it's pretty clear where things land in this case. The WOD-news-show with its vamily-spotlight is an <i>official product</i>. So your scenario of an independent channel called &quot;ChicagoByNightLover&quot; is irrelevant as that isn't what we're talking about.<br /> <br /> And even then, <i>an independent Youtube-channel should also ask for permission first</i> and have some correspondence with an artist before using their art. It's just that official channels should be expected to be even more careful and courteous when it comes to fan-interactions. Because official channels should come with a raised expectation of quality in production and ethical conduct.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for explaining. Much appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T21:07:29-08:00","id":1530243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530151-is-white-wolf-paradox-stealing-art-now?p=1530222#post1530222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fan content license is, if I remember, fairly specific, so would not generally apply, for instance, to pictures published on a blog or similar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh the Dark Pack redux was hugely flawed because it was meant to be one of three different content licenses to cover different kinds of content, but they only did the first and thus all fan content would have to fall under it or not take part in it; which is part of the reason so few fans used it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But the fact that the art is specifically referencing the intellectual property of Paradox would make a fair use argument pretty strong if the matter ever went to court, or, indeed, another form of adjudication. </div> </div> </div>There's nothing in IP law that states that derivative works are inherently less protected when the owner of the IP derived from is involved.<br /> <br /> If I make a fan documentary on the World of Darkness, and I monetize it on YouTube, and then Paradox reuploads it to their YouTube account, or streams in on their Twitch account, the fact that I made a film about the WoD has no bearing on a claim of fair use by Paradox. In the eyes of the law it would be no different if my subject matter was the Pokemon franchise and Paradox did the same thing. Paradox's fair use claim would have to be justified under the principles of fair use on its own merits.<br /> <br /> Sure, because IP law is very judge dependent some judges might give weight to the IP owner regarding a dispute over fan materials because there is very little restraint on IP judges, but it's not a stronger case on the letter of the law (or even the spirit of it).<br /> <br /> The only stronger position Paradox has as the IP owner is if they want to stop a fan work; which is not the case at hand.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530151-is-white-wolf-paradox-stealing-art-now?p=1530224#post1530224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, there is a simple answer; it falls under the criticism and comment area of fair use as defined by section 107 of the US Copyright Act.<br /> <br /> (There are actually quite a few avenues for fair use, and a transformation is only one.)</div> </div> </div> </div>This is completely incorrect.<br /> <br /> Transformation (or the four considerations listed in section 107 as more codified tests of fair use) is how you tell if something is validly one of the kinds of fair use. There is no other &quot;avenue&quot; of fair use.<br /> <br /> If I posted a video of me &quot;criticizing and commenting&quot; on a full length feature film where I show the whole film and then at the end I say, &quot;I hated that.&quot; I would most likely lose utterly in a fair use defense. I did not transform the content in any meaningful fashion. Yes, I criticized and commented, but not enough to claim my use of copyrighted material was fair use.<br /> <br /> If I recorded a rolling commentary of everything I hated about the movie with detailed explanations and examples over the entire duration, I'd actually have a case (though not a slam dunk case, it would at least be a case the court would take seriously). Even better if multiple aspects are relevant (cinematography, CGI elements, audio, etc) to further make the case that the whole thing was important to transform with my voice over.<br /> <br /> Just asserting that what Paradox did falls under criticism and commentary is not sufficient to call it fair use. That's why section 107 immediately proceeds to how to adjudicate the grey areas of how much transformation is enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T22:45:56-08:00","id":1530245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530151-is-white-wolf-paradox-stealing-art-now?p=1530223#post1530223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You should want to build a friendly rapport with the fan-base. When somebody puts in the work to produce fan-art, the IP-holder's attitude shouldn't be &quot;And now it's mine, you fool!&quot;. The artist in question acted as a fan and wanted to express their appreciation for an IP. So it's only fair to call for some consideration and courtesy when it comes to the interaction with fans. The IP-holder gets something out of the art-work being produced and the least one can do is also treat the artist behind that like a person.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that's not really what has happened. They never said or behaved like appropriating a property: they showed It for a minute, complemented the artist and credited It and gave a massive spotlight for nothing to someone who Is actually behaving as an assholes.<br /> <br /> The artist in question quite evidente acted as an exalted edition warrior, and decided to raise the incredible &quot;theft&quot; accusation because helds the belief that Wod20 Is a separate property, never evil Paradox dare to touch It with her unclean hands.<br /> <br /> I mean, it's literally written in the message.<br /> <br /> Idk how we can blame Outstar of bad behaviour, when she was literally accused of committing a crime. Doesn't this seem not treating her as a person? Did the artist try to reach out with her and clarify her position?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T00:39:13-08:00","id":1530251,"title":"","content":"It's rather sad to see people simping for a company with billions in assets to the point of making up ridiculous narratives to dehumanize and belittle a fan artist.<br /> <br /> No amount of attacking a fan artist is going to make Paradox care you exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T01:14:43-08:00","id":1530254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530151-is-white-wolf-paradox-stealing-art-now?p=1530251#post1530251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's rather sad to see people simping for a company with billions in assets to the point of making up ridiculous narratives to dehumanize and belittle a fan artist.<br /> <br /> No amount of attacking a fan artist is going to make Paradox care you exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is ... Not an argument at all? Just a strawman bordering on personal attack?<br /> <br /> It's rather sad to see people sistematically slandering other fans and engaged authors and freelancers who are just working under the wrong (according to your parameters) Company.<br /> <br /> Because let me remind you that Paradox gave this whole project to die-hard fans of the brand, including Outstar herself, and has involved lots of people with a history with Vtm and Wod.<br /> <br /> And no amount of calling them Nazis, edgelords, thieves, racists and other defamatory and derogatory terme will cancel this fact.<br /> <br /> By the way, I'm sure as fuck was treated better by supposedly evil Paradox people, online, than by supposedly inclusive OPP fans on this forum, by whom I'm constantly belittled for liking the wrong edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 02-08-2024, 04:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":4},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T01:58:28-08:00","id":1530259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530151-is-white-wolf-paradox-stealing-art-now?p=1530245#post1530245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But that's not really what has happened. They never said or behaved like appropriating a property: they showed It for a minute, complemented the artist and credited It and gave a massive spotlight for nothing to someone who Is actually behaving as an assholes.<br /> <br /> The artist in question quite evidente acted as an exalted edition warrior, and decided to raise the incredible &quot;theft&quot; accusation because helds the belief that Wod20 Is a separate property, never evil Paradox dare to touch It with her unclean hands.<br /> <br /> I mean, it's literally written in the message.<br /> <br /> Idk how we can blame Outstar of bad behaviour, when she was literally accused of committing a crime. Doesn't this seem not treating her as a person? Did the artist try to reach out with her and clarify her position?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is what the process should be like:<ul><li>You look around the web and look for WOD-fan-art you want to show off during the show.</li> <li>You contact the artist and ask them whether their work can be featured on the show for free.</li> <li>At this step, it's also entirely acceptable for the artist to say &quot;No, I don't want my art to be shown on your show.&quot;. And that's it. You move on and talk to another artist about whether they want to be featured on the show.</li> <li>If the artist agrees, you ask the artist how they want to be represented on the show (their name (if for example they want their real name and not just their internet-username to be mentioned), art-page, maybe a shout-out for a Patreon etc.).</li> <li>The name and relevant links aren't just in the show but then are also reproduced in the description of the YT-video.</li> </ul>That's what the process <i>should be</i> <i>like</i>. And I think deviating from this is a mistake, a bad practice that disrespects the artists in question and as mentioned before just invites disaster at some point (this thread is a case in point for that).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T02:23:52-08:00","id":1530261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530151-is-white-wolf-paradox-stealing-art-now?p=1530254#post1530254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is ... Not an argument at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct. There's no point in arguing with you when you read a post that contains no negative statements about V5, includes positive statements about enjoying any edition you like, and is about how an official Paradox production is acting as an edition war.<br /> <br /> Arguments are for people that want a rational discussion, not for people that want to read edition wars into things to belittle others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because let me remind you that Paradox gave this whole project to die-hard fans of the brand, including Outstar herself, and has involved lots of people with a history with Vtm and Wod. </div> </div> </div>Saying &quot;gave&quot; instead of &quot;sold&quot; or &quot;monetized&quot; is the kind of semantic bullshit that gets people called corporate simps.<br /> <br /> Paradox hasn't given us anything. They are selling a product. I don't need to call them names (some of which they've certainly earned) because their promotional material doesn't have the right o use copyrighted material other people made without permission. I understand you're itching to make more of it than this so you can get push back and then justify your delusions of persecution, but that's just demonstrating that there's no point in seriously engaging in a debate with you about this.<br /> <br /> You're not actually making arguments, you're throwing punches and hoping someone punches back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T10:42:31-08:00","id":1530288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530151-is-white-wolf-paradox-stealing-art-now?p=1530261#post1530261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Saying &quot;gave&quot; instead of &quot;sold&quot; or &quot;monetized&quot; is the kind of semantic bullshit that gets people called corporate simps.<br /> <br /> Paradox hasn't given us anything. They are selling a product. I don't need to call them names (some of which they've certainly earned) because their promotional material doesn't have the right o use copyrighted material other people made without permission. I understand you're itching to make more of it than this so you can get push back and then justify your delusions of persecution, but that's just demonstrating that there's no point in seriously engaging in a debate with you about this.<br /> <br /> You're not actually making arguments, you're throwing punches and hoping someone punches back.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're mis-interpreting my words, as it often happens, perhaps it's my rusty written english.<br /> <br /> Paradox hasn't given us anything besides books to buy: what I was saying is that Wod5e was and is managed, written and communicated by a good number of long-time fans and old-time authors and freelancers: Martin Ericsson, Karim Muhammar, Jason Carl, Justin Achilli, Outstar, Matthew Dawkins and the freelancers who worked for him when he was Creative Lead, Khaldoun Khelil, Greg Stolze ... they are all people whose love of the brand is evident, and many of them have contributed a lot to the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> I'm not forgetting that these people are and were fans, that they are also professionals and human beings, and in a lot of discussions I see, many of them are constanyl belittled, offended, dehumanized and slandered.<br /> <br /> If you think I'm a corporate simp because I don't take for granted that Outstar has committed a crime, then I'm a corporate simp. However, you should very much review your definition of &quot;double standards&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 02-08-2024, 01:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T11:15:48-08:00","id":1530293,"title":"","content":"The good news is that changes are being implemented (from Outstar's <a href=\"https://twitter.com/outstarwalker/status/1755615619750535676\" target=\"_blank\">Twitter</a>):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, we're making some changes.<br /> <br /> From now on, the only creators we will show, praise and promote on the stream will be the ones who contact us, or respond to our reach out.<br /> <br /> This will have an unfortunate and immediate effect of less creators being featured, at least at first. </div> </div> </div>That's the right decision and it's good to see that she listened to the criticism.<br /> <br /> The bad news is that Outstar then proceeded to start a beef with a YT-content-creator... sigh","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T11:40:46-08:00","id":1530295,"title":"","content":"Does anyone know how to contact them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T11:48:08-08:00","id":1530296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530151-is-white-wolf-paradox-stealing-art-now?p=1530295#post1530295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone know how to contact them?</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume the best place for it would be the official Discord-server. Using the &quot;# vamily&quot; hashtag probably will also help.<br /> <br /> The way I've seen it handled in the past by podcasts or websites is either setting up a contact-formular on a website or having a dedicated email-address for submissions. Maybe they will arrange something like that in the near future. So that's maybe something to be on the lookout for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T11:56:57-08:00","id":1530297,"title":"","content":"Reading the Outstar Twitter thread (Twitter is always a hellscape so I shouldn't be surprised) is depressing as fuck, especially with all the threats to WOD employees and calls for violence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T12:03:14-08:00","id":1530298,"title":"","content":"Seems pretty simple to me. This is why Critical Role no longer showcases art and why bigger companies have releases for any promotional use of fanmade art on their socials. While Paradox is the owner of the IP, the artist is the owner of the art and they have final say how and where it can be featured. Is the &quot;Vamily&quot; useage within fair use is kinda complicated as it was used on something meant to market Paradox products and that is monetised on different streaming services. This means that there should be a conversation about this at the least.<br /> <br /> Sidenote, am I the only one who finds the term &quot;Vamily&quot; horrifyingly cringe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T12:05:11-08:00","id":1530299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530151-is-white-wolf-paradox-stealing-art-now?p=1530298#post1530298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems pretty simple to me. This is why Critical Role no longer showcases art and why bigger companies have releases for any promotional use of fanmade art on their socials. While Paradox is the owner of the IP, the artist is the owner of the art and they have final say how and where it can be featured. Is the &quot;Vamily&quot; useage within fair use is kinda complicated as it was used on something meant to market Paradox products and that is monetised on different streaming services. This means that there should be a conversation about this at the least.<br /> <br /> Sidenote, am I the only one who finds the term &quot;Vamily&quot; horrifyingly cringe?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a twitter hashtag designed to be small so you can post more content.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/