even if it's necessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T12:25:40-08:00","id":1530307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530151-is-white-wolf-paradox-stealing-art-now?p=1530297#post1530297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading the Outstar Twitter thread (Twitter is always a hellscape so I shouldn't be surprised) is depressing as fuck, especially with all the threats to WOD employees and calls for violence.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was no need for her to put one specific content-creator on blast... sigh This post from the artist at the beginning of this thread caused some controversy which thankfully has led to these much-needed changes. Now it's time for deescalation rather than stirring up new drama. Singling out one particular person and attacking them only makes things worse. Getting into heated arguments about these topics... That's what people like you and me do in threads like this one here. She's supposed to be the WOD-community-developer.<br /> <br /> I don't envy Outstar her position, of course. Since Justin Achilli left, outside of Jason Carl occasionally making a public appearance, Outstar is the sole public face of WOD under Paradox's management. I don't really agree with how this is handled and I think Paradox should give Outstar more support or better yet hire more people to deal with the PR-side of things. Instead, the way things are handled now Paradox is just burdening her alone with handling the WOD-news-show, being the WOD-community-developer <i>and </i>being the sole public face of the WOD. And the way Paradox has been handling the IP hasn't exactly gone smoothly, so during all of that being the community-developer overseeing all of the trials and tribulations, all the back and forths or arguments within the community while <i>also </i>being the sole public face of the WOD wasn't a pleasant experience, I imagine.<br /> <br /> Outstar starting a mudslinging-contest with a YT-content-creator doesn't do anything except give rise to cheap drama which will just deteriorate the general mood of the WOD-community even more. The person from the tumblr-post from the beginning of this thread is already complaining about how Outstar has wrongfully singled out that Youtube-guy for starting the whole thing. God, this kind of drama never leads to anything good...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T12:54:38-08:00","id":1530310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530151-is-white-wolf-paradox-stealing-art-now?p=1530299#post1530299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a twitter hashtag designed to be small so you can post more content.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem isn't the &quot;V&quot; it's the &quot;family.&quot;<br /> <br /> This is a fairly on-the-nose example of parasocial marketing: obfuscating the consumer/seller relationship behind the idea of a deeper intimate relationship with a fictional entity (corporations are not people, professional media personalities are putting on personas as part of their job, etc.) to instill loyalty to a brand beyond a normal consumer relationship. If you're part of the &quot;Paradox WoD family,&quot; you start supporting and defending Paradox and the WoD team like family members instead of people selling you things. And yes, not everyone falls into it, but the parasocial effect is very real and effective.<br /> <br /> This is nothing new in the worlds of brands and marketing; see team sports as a business. But the social media era has exacerbated this a lot by having more direct interaction between companies/brands/paid marketing individuals and consumers creating a greater sense of deeper interactions instead of it still being a sales pitch, as well as algorithmic targeting resulting in social media bubbles that make parasocial bonding happen at a vastly accelerated rate.<br /> <br /> <br /> --------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Outstar is also adding to the mess by claiming that all fan art falls under the Dark Pack rules even though the Dark Pack rules explicitly state otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T14:10:21-08:00","id":1530312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530151-is-white-wolf-paradox-stealing-art-now?p=1530251#post1530251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's rather sad to see people simping for a company with billions in assets to the point of making up ridiculous narratives to dehumanize and belittle a fan artist.<br /> <br /> No amount of attacking a fan artist is going to make Paradox care you exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's crazy times indeed where making personal attacks on somebody you might disagree with is perfectly okay and this is why I'm barely on social media and have become more selective in my youtube viewing. Personal attacks don't accomplish but make people feel more isolated and it's partly why I don't watch many products from Hollywood anymore as social media has killed the movie star so to speak.<br /> <br /> I should add I find it funny that people are getting bent out shape when actors and actresses take roles in movies that may flop or have the &quot;Message&quot; (Decided to channel Critical Drinker here.) Did people forget that acting is a job and they may not have the same attachment to said characters you might have?<br /> <br /> Or the fact it's a fact that movies are shot out of sequence and scripts can changed dramatically by the time the principle cast have shot the first scene.<br /> <br /> I remember something that Michael Caine said why he would take certain roles as it was a job and wanted the money to that effect.<br /> <br /> Actually it's was in response why he did one of the Jaws sequals and in essence it's was<br /> <br /> &quot; I never watched the movie and I heard it's bad, but the house I got from the job was beautiful.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 02-08-2024, 05:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T15:10:09-08:00","id":1530318,"title":"","content":"The onerous is not on Paradox to make a community into a family, the onerous is on the community. We have an obligation to support and uplift one another as well as respect each other's love of the setting as well as product,<br /> <br /> We're not employees, we're people who come together because we all love the same fictional universe.<br /> <br /> Violent threats against one another is vile and hopefully we can realize we should all show basic human respect and decency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T15:34:04-08:00","id":1530320,"title":"","content":"I think being a fan means being in love with a fictional setting and elements of that fiction as they have been represented in media. But being a fan should include a critical perspective of said media and a continued reevaluation of said media over time. You like what you like but being a fan should never mean to feel beholden to what one likes. It's always important to examine why you like a thing and your relationship to that thing. Especially once commercial products get involved. There's the thing you like that exists in your mind and there's the product some company is trying to sell you. These should never be treated as the same thing. The thing you like should be determined by your perception of it and not some sales-pitch from a greedy company looking to make a profit.<br /> <br /> Being a fan of something doesn't mean supporting a company that tries to sell you something in every way. That's why threads like this one are important. Somebody fucked up, the fan-community calls them out and a change for the better occurs in reaction to that. This is a good thing.<br /> <br /> PS: As for the other stuff... I find it a bit curious how this all started with a show badly handling their artist-showcases and then this pivot to complaining about social-media-conduct occurred. Sure, it happens and it's bad. But what has that got to do with the original complaint? Absolutely nothing of course. Just curious why this irrelevant dramabait was thrown into the mix here...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T15:51:52-08:00","id":1530322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530151-is-white-wolf-paradox-stealing-art-now?p=1530320#post1530320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">PS: As for the other stuff... I find it a bit curious how this all started with a show badly handling their artist-showcases and then this pivot to complaining about social-media-conduct occurred. Sure, it happens and it's bad. But what has that got to do with the original complaint? Absolutely nothing of course. Just curious why this irrelevant dramabait was thrown into the mix here...</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean the argument isn't just whether or not White Wolf did something wrong. The argument is whether or not one side or the other attacked someone.<br /> <br /> I mean, if you dismiss threats of violence and harrassment, you're burying the lead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T16:01:16-08:00","id":1530324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530151-is-white-wolf-paradox-stealing-art-now?p=1530322#post1530322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean the argument isn't just whether or not White Wolf did something wrong. The argument is whether or not one side or the other attacked someone.<br /> <br /> I mean, if you dismiss threats of violence and harrassment, you're burying the lead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, strange way to phrase this because your post presents a prime example of &quot;burying the lead&quot;. Because isn't it strange how you suddenly argue &quot;argument isn't just whether or not White Wolf did something wrong&quot;. No, that pretty much is at the heart of this issue. After all, that's why Outstar issued a correction and announced that the way artists are dealt with by the vamily-segment has changed. That's what this has been about. It's also what we've been discussing in the thread so far, you might notice. A fuck-up occured, the community complained and the offical WOD-news-show responded to the backlash for its mistake by changing its policy. That's what has happened.<br /> <br /> People saying nasty things on social media has absolutely nothing to do with that. It's a completely separate issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T16:38:25-08:00","id":1530326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530151-is-white-wolf-paradox-stealing-art-now?p=1530318#post1530318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The onerous is not on Paradox to make a community into a family, the onerous is on the community. We have an obligation to support and uplift one another as well as respect each other's love of the setting as well as product,</div> </div> </div> </div>The onerous is on nobody? I'd actually rather nobody tried to turn fandoms into families. That is the problem. Paradox is trying to artificially create a &quot;chosen family&quot; by manipulating fans into desiring that instead of having a more healthy relationship with the product, the company, and the community. Not only is it not their onerous, it's not a good thing for the community. It's a good thing for marketing. Paradox isn't some special bad guy here, it's an extremely common marketing strategy from individual Internet content creators to megacorps.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Violent threats against one another is vile and hopefully we can realize we should all show basic human respect and decency. </div> </div> </div>Yes, but we shouldn't try to distract from our bad behavior by pointing at irrelevant bad behavior by someone else. We also shouldn't over state social media language. Nobody is actually threatening to gather up the W5 team and feeding them to wolves.<br /> <br /> Additionally, it's important to not take social media posts that have been screen capped and stripped of all context (except that they were responses to one poster) including who even said them, as fitting the narrative of the person that did such information muddying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T16:51:50-08:00","id":1530327,"title":"","content":"I am sorry, but my OCD is killing me.<br /> We are talking about<br /> <br /> <b>onus - </b>Burden<br /> not<br /> <b>onerous</b> - problematic, troublesome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T17:38:46-08:00","id":1530328,"title":"","content":"I thought it was intended to be onus, but I also didn't even clock that wasn't the word being used...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T17:51:58-08:00","id":1530329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530151-is-white-wolf-paradox-stealing-art-now?p=1530328#post1530328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought it was intended to be onus, but I also didn't even clock that wasn't the word being used...</div> </div> </div> </div>I understood that from your response, just couldn't bear further repetition of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T18:00:28-08:00","id":1530330,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry,I dont understand. I legitimately don't. A lot of YouTube post fan art that people made of them in social media, a lot of social media pages about books and TV shows share fan art people make about their characters and it's OK. Why is it not OK when Outstar does it?<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1182_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1182\" data-vbnamecard=\"1182\">Asmodai</a> I know I butted heads with you two before so I I wanna clarify I'm legitimately asking i ngood faith. How is Outstar showing a drawing of a vtm vampire someone made different than say The SpongeBob Twitter account sharing a drawing of SpongeBob a little kind made?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T18:17:45-08:00","id":1530332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530151-is-white-wolf-paradox-stealing-art-now?p=1530330#post1530330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry,I dont understand. I legitimately don't. A lot of YouTube post fan art that people made of them in social media, a lot of social media pages about books and TV shows share fan art people make about their characters and it's OK. Why is it not OK when Outstar does it?<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1182_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1182\" data-vbnamecard=\"1182\">Asmodai</a> I know I butted heads with you two before so I I wanna clarify I'm legitimately asking i ngood faith. How is Outstar showing a drawing of a vtm vampire someone made different than say The SpongeBob Twitter account sharing a drawing of SpongeBob a little kind made?</div> </div> </div> </div>From the Nick accounts? Little, and that's presumably the issue, because Nickolodeon is a part of a huge corporation that slings around a lot of money. When a lot of money is added to the equation, things stop being fun and start becoming serious fucking business. This isn't a small, indie Vtuber operation; it's an arm of a formal business of notable size.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T18:27:14-08:00","id":1530333,"title":"","content":"I think I get it know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-08T20:40:48-08:00","id":1530341,"title":"","content":"So...<br /> <br /> 1) Most bigger companies rely on fan-submissions for such efforts. Spongebob can ask for fan submissions and get enough submissions to post a fan work every 15 minutes for the next few decades. I haven't specifically looked up the Spongebob Twitter account, but Nickelodeon has been doing these things since I was a young kid and it was always fan submissions to get your drawings on TV/etc. Fan-submissions also come with a bunch of fine-print legalese to establish what rights are being waived/exchanged.<br /> <br /> 2) Most smaller content creators that do this already abide by the general guidelines Knightingale posted in post 34. While not universal this general attitude is basically what keeps the Internet's creative spaces from devolving into everyone pulling their art and being in dozens of different lawsuits. It's a set of general norms most creators agree to in order to meet a level of socially agreed to &quot;don't sue folks&quot; status quo (because again, IP laws, not just in the US, are woefully behind the speed at which the Internet operates).<br /> <br /> 3) As has been noted, small creators that get big often end up changing their sharing habits because getting big enough creates a number of problems and the easiest solution is to stop doing these sorts of fan appreciation sections (esp, if you're not so big you can do submissions forever).<br /> <br /> 4) As noted, the situation in question is one where it's not one small creator sharing the works of another small creator as part of a mutually beneficial community. It's a for-profit company using fan art without permission for their own advertising purposes and no considerations to how the creators they feature want to be exposed to a larger audience (though it's actually a very small audience.. so it's not even a great case for getting &quot;exposure&quot; to the wider WoD community when most of the WoD News videos get less than 5K views).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 02-09-2024, 02:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-09T02:03:10-08:00","id":1530351,"title":"","content":"Ok....had to go look up this 'violence' thing because knowing the Youtuber in question that makes zero sense.......and it seems their great crime was using a British slang euphemism for ' take a look at their behviour' or ' pay attention to what they are doing'.<br /> <br /> I'm just glad I've never used any Australian slang when communicating with these folks I'd probably end up on a watchlist or something with the amount of misinterpretation ( deliberate or no) thats being done....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-09T02:11:32-08:00","id":1530353,"title":"","content":"I think to showcase the issue: Somebody responded to the original tumblr-post with this<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> mentemori<br /> I gotta say it did feel very violating to have the relationship between my tzimisce and their ghoul \u2014 played by me and my best friend respectively \u2014 speculated on and discussed within the spotlight segment. They never got our permission \u2014 and it just feels kinda icky to have the dynamic of a oc ship broadcasted on that kind of platform without the original creators being able to provide context </div> </div> </div>Of course, Outstar and Huddy weren't intentionally making this awkward. They just didn't know the context of the art-piece. Or imagine if somebody were to draw characters whose looks are modeled after real-life friends, then it gets shown on the show without that context and now making a comment about the looks of the drawn people has a very different meaning to it with the actual context in mind. And then there's the issue of artists talking about in that thread how they only found out about the show after this controversy started only to then figure out that their art had already been shown off multiple times. But when these artists posted their art they weren't even aware of the show's existence. The change was absolutely necessary.<br /> <br /> And a way to make sure the amount of art shown off doesn't decrease, you can't just wait for people to send in art who want to be featured on the show but you also have to do some outreach and talk to artists who may not even be aware of the show's existence. The controversy has shown that there's quite a few artists who just didn't even know of the show to begin with. But that outreach takes time and effort which brings me back to the part of Outstar not getting enough support. If the show could get another hire who's just there as a producer then that would already make the show less of a burden for Outstar alone. Of course, from the way it worked in the past, I doubt that part will change.<br /> <br /> _______________________________________<br /> <br /> I've also been thinking about Outstar calling out the YT-content-creator and I'm now convinced that it was simply a bad move. If it were purely about the bad tone of social media posts why not scratch out all the usernames in order to just highlight the tone of the posts? Why would you instead scratch out all the usernames - except for one? It would also be a preposterous notion to make one person singlehandedly responsible for all comments made on Twitter, for example. The whole thing instead comes off as quite vindictive as the issue, it seems, isn't even the tone of the posts but her personal beef with this one person. Who knows what the history is there and who said what and when... Something like that should be resolved in private only. It's not like how by dragging this out into the open the YT-content-creator is gonna be like &quot;You know, now that you said all that negative stuff about me in public, I'm gonna do a 180 and completely change my attitude towards you.&quot;. Of course, that won't happen. If anything, this just made it even worse. And even if talking to the person in private (via DMs or something) doesn't work, then you just have to swallow down your anger, block the guy and move on. No good comes from stuff like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-09T03:39:54-08:00","id":1530357,"title":"","content":"As some people appear confused:<br /> <br /> - Paradox makes a community spotlight show where they spotlight community work without asking permission.<br /> - Some members of the community are fine with this, others aren't.<br /> - Paradox should have sought permission beforehand. My suspicion is that Outstar and Huddy looked through Twitter, Tumblr, Instagram, etc. for this art and collected it for their show without seeking approval from their bosses, because they didn't consider someone who creates fan art would object to their art being spotlit. This was an error.<br /> - Realising their error, Paradox confirm they will seek permission in future.<br /> - One vlogger in particular puts the company and Outstar on blast for this error, which has been identified as a trend behaviour by this individual.<br /> - As part of the &quot;blast&quot; some people mockingly advocate punishment (some implying physical violence, though usually stated with comical exaggeration, YMMV) for the identified wrongdoers - Outstar and Huddy, in this case.<br /> - People who respond badly to threats of violence, joking or not (&quot;it's just a joke!&quot;, &quot;this insult isn't offensive to me, so it shouldn't be to you!&quot;, and &quot;it's a harmless term in my country!&quot; aren't legitimate defences in many eyes these days) call out the vlogger for bad behaviour and request these threats stop, citing their hurt feelings.<br /> - Outstar notes this perpetual antagonism is something they tried to resolve privately with the vlogger on multiple occasions, but without success.<br /> - The fans have now in part pivoted away from the original issue and are taking stands based on whether they think Outstar and Huddy expressing their hurt feelings and admonishment of the vlogger is appropriate, while others concentrate on the subject of using fan art without permission.<br /> <br /> Sidenote: As mentioned, it's &quot;onus&quot; and &quot;burying the lede.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's quite possible for multiple parties to be in the wrong here, and nobody needs to lick boots or burn down a company to make their point. Paradox should have sought permission and will apparently be doing so in future. Fans should not even be jokingly advocating for violence against a community manager or their team, because some people take it seriously, and you don't know the experience of the person you're mocking in this way. Was it a calculated move to distract from the fan art issue to call out this vlogger? I doubt it. I suspect that the stress of being under fire for this error, and from a source that persistently complains about the way you're doing your job, is enough to make you think &quot;This isn't fair, and I'm going to speak out about it.&quot;<br /> <br /> People don't always act calmly and resolve things quietly, and sometimes it feels like you can't. People act emotionally and say things they shouldn't. Because it's on social media it's magnified into a greater issue than it would otherwise be. This is a simple situation that's blown up, and I'd suggest each participant in the &quot;feud&quot; returns to their corner and refocuses on something positive and creative instead of trying to score points against their opponent.<br /> <br /> It all makes me very glad I'm no longer the World of Darkness community manager, frankly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-09T18:49:35-08:00","id":1530416,"title":"","content":"I'd like to thank everyone for their patience with me,I did not understand situation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-09T22:01:40-08:00","id":1530422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Paradox should have sought permission and will appa